id: pm-tpwde6
title: "GH-859: pm-beads source export can omit Beads comment bodies and events"
description: "The current Beads export consumed by pm-beads may omit comment bodies and event history, so migration can appear successful while losing context. The importer must either consume a lossless source or emit a fail-closed completeness receipt before writing PM records."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:extensions",comments,history,migration,pm-beads
created_at: "2026-08-02T14:10:55.004Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-14T10:15:03.728Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: A source fixture with comments and events imports every body and event with record/content parity; incomplete export formats fail closed with actionable guidance; immutable backup and source/target parity gates are documented and tested; package and installed-consumer acceptance pass
goal: project management = context management
objective: Guarantee lossless Beads-to-pm context migration
value: Prevents silent loss of discussion and history during importer adoption
why_now: GitHub issue #859 reports a live migration data-loss boundary
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: high
confidence: 95
